==Battleground==
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 8~13.33 seconds<sup>240f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 8~13.33 seconds<sup>240f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 266.67 seconds<sup>8,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**Infinite [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cats]] spawn, delay 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**30 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 2~6.67 seconds<sup>60f~200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]'s Normal and Evolved Forms are useless since they are outranged by the Loincloth Cats and him being too slow. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] are recommended since they only get knocked back when they die. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] or Cyberpunk Cat is ideal for his long range. Stall the Loincloth Cats with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Wall Cat]], as their damage is pretty low. Just meatshield with Crazed Tank Cat, Eraser Cat, and Crazed Macho Cat, and use one [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attacker]] for the Doge Darks and Gabriels.

